<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			13/3/97		   6/3/97	     15/3/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	    550			550		   650</p>
<p>    Naphtha	     100		   75-100		    75</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   1,750		    1,750		 1,800</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	300-325			375		   375</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     15		    15-20		    10</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks were steady with rapid throughput of incoming cargoes and departing barges as well as cargoes heading to the Med and across the Atlantic.</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks rose slightly with incoming cargoes.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks were balanced as product came ex-FSU and departed in barges. Market contango is set to encourage stock building, but IPE delivery material will mostly go to Germany.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks fell with FSU straight-run material arriving, while some left for Germany in barges. Cracked material headed for other NWE ports.</p>
<p>Jet fuel stocks fell as the aviation sector took product.</p>
</text>
